{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 32, :comments ["<b>For it was harat the way before me.</b> Our Sages, the rabbis of the Mishnah, expounded it as a notarikon — יראה, ראתה, נטתה: because the way was before me (Shabbat 105a) — that is, out of jealousy for me and to provoke me. And according to its plain sense: כי חרד הדרך לנגדי — a term of trembling — for I saw that the master of the way was alarmed and hastened on the way that is to my anger and my defiance, and the verse is elliptical, like ״וַתֵּכַל דָּוִד״ (II Samuel 13). Another interpretation: ירט is a term of appeasement, and so ״עַל יְדֵי רְשָׁעִים יִרְטֵנִי״ (Job 16) — he appeases and comforts me through the wicked, who are nothing but provokers."], :book :numbers, :voice :rashi, :lang :en, :chapter 22, :notes {}, :source-witnesses nil, :timestamp "2026-08-02T09:12:18.294033798Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}